$CATEGORY: top/Quizbot/demo/c1 Anatomy and purpose of a for loop
// Anatomy and purpose of a for loop

// [id:c1-A] [tag:c1] [tag:multiple_choice]
::c1-A Naming the three components::What are the three components required within the parentheses of a for loop? {
    ~Start value, End value, and Step size
    =Initialization, Condition, and Incrementer
    ~Variable declaration, Boolean expression, and Update rule
    ~Start value, End value, and Incrementer
}

// [id:c1-B] [tag:c1] [tag:multiple_choice]
::c1-B Which part controls continuation::Which part of the for loop determines if the loop continues or stops? {
    =The Condition
    ~The Initialization
    ~The Incrementer
    ~The Code Block
}

// [id:c1-C] [tag:c1] [tag:multiple_choice]
::c1-C Purpose of the incrementer::In `for (let x \= 0; x < 10; x++)`, what is the purpose of `x++`? {
    ~To set the starting value of x
    ~To check if x is less than 10
    ~To define the range of the loop
    =To update the variable after each iteration
}

// [id:c1-D] [tag:c1] [tag:multiple_choice]
::c1-D Omitting the incrementer::What happens if you omit the incrementer in a for loop? {
    ~The code throws a syntax error
    ~The loop runs once
    =You create an infinite loop because the variable never changes
    ~The loop increments by 1 automatically
}

